      "text": "1. **Identifying the form of fractions:**\n\n   Given the equation,\n   \\[\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i},\\]\n\n   both fractions are of the form \\(a + 5i\\) and \\(b - 5i\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are complex numbers. Specifically,\n   \\[\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)},\\]\n   \\[\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}.\\]\n\n2. **Simplifying the denominators:**\n\n   Since \\(3 - (-5i) = 3 + 5i\\) and \\(3 - 5i\\) are complex conjugates, the denominator becomes,\n   \\[(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 + (-5i)^2 = 9 + 25(-1) = 9 - 25 = -16.\\]\n\n   So, we have,\n   \\[\\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{-16} + \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{-16} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2 + (3 - 5i)^2}{-16}.\\]\n\n3. **Evaluating numerator:\\\n\n   The numerator can be expanded and simplified:\n   \\[(3 + 5i)^2 + (3 - 5i)^2 = \\left(3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2\\right) + \\left(3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (-5i)^2\\right).\\]\n\n   This simplifies to,\n   \\[9 + 30i - 25 + 3^2 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 3^2 - 25 - 25 = 81 - 75 = 3.\\]\n\n4. **Putting it all together:**\n\n   With \\((3 + 5i)^2 + (3 - 5i)^2 = 3 \\neq 0,\\)\n   \\[\\frac{3}{-16} = -\\frac{3}{16}.\\]\n\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\\boxed{\\text{-}\\frac{3}{16}}.\\]",
